<article class="env-remark" id="294A7A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/294A7A">Remark <span data-tag="294A7A">8.1.4.3</span>.</a> Let $G: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a right-lax monoidal functor between monoidal categories. Suppose that $\calD $ is a category enriched over $\calC $. We may define a category $G(\calD )$, enriched over $\calC '$, as follows: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The objects of $G(\calD )$ are the objects of $\calD $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Given objects $X,Y \in \calD $, we set 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \bHom _{G(\calD )}(X,Y) = G( \bHom _{\calD }(X,Y) ). \]
</div>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
The composition in $G(\calD )$ is given by the map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  G( \bHom _{\calD }(Y,Z) ) \otimes G( \bHom _{\calD }(X,Y) ) \rightarrow G( \bHom _{\calD }(Y,Z) \otimes \bHom _{\calD }(X,Y) ) \rightarrow G( \bHom _{\calD }(X,Z)). \]
</div>
<p>
 Here the first map is determined by the right-weakly monoidal structure on the functor $G$, and the second is obtained by applying $G$ to the composition law in the category $\calD $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
For every object $X \in \calD $, the associated unit $G(\calD )$ is given by the composition 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  {\bf 1_{\calC '} } \rightarrow G( { \bf 1_{\calC } } ) \rightarrow G( \bHom _{\calD }(X,X)). \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>